Registered SRAM outputs (SRAM_OUT_REG) - gates and cycle cost, 2026-10-17
=========================================================================

Branch sram-out-reg on fork main 5efc69b (PR #28). Host: 48 cores, load
~100-200 throughout (shared), so wall times are pessimistic. Verilator
5.048 (deps/) unless noted. "OREG=0/1" = SRAM_OUT_REG of the TB top.

== Design ==
SRAM_OUT_REG=1 registers the read output of all 15 SRAM arrays (3 VRF
replicas, 6 L1 data ways, 6 L1 tag ways): read data valid two cycles
after the read. Default 1 in the ORFS macro builds (MUSERISC_SRAM_FAKERAM45 /
MUSERISC_SRAM_SKY130), 0 otherwise. Consumers:
  - muserisc_sram_sp / muserisc_vrf_bank: capture register = output
    register (macro dout -> flop, no logic); behavioural model adds the
    same register; vregfile full-word bypass delayed one cycle.
  - muserisc_vec: SR read-wait stage between S0 and S1 (one element per
    cycle kept), S1 skid copies of the read words when S1 does not
    advance in its first cycle, vrgather.vv second read waits a cycle,
    old-vd currency tracked through SR.
  - muserisc_core vector LS sequencer: VLS_RW wait after a RD cycle that
    read the VRF.
  - muserisc_icache / muserisc_dcache: S_RDW lookup wait; D$ write-back
    read and FENCE.I tag read one more cycle; I$ two-entry fetch buffer
    (last responded doubleword + next doubleword prefetched in the
    response cycle) answering in one cycle.

