Where the Linux cost comes from: boot to the first "RCU Tasks Trace"
line, soc_tb latency 1, with one cache forced back to SRAM_OUT_REG=0
(experiment builds, not committed):
  OREG=0                                 1,270,996,565
  OREG=1                                 1,708,257,220   +34.4 %
  OREG=1, D$ arrays unregistered         1,365,241,323   +7.4 %  (= I$ share)
  OREG=1, I$ arrays unregistered         1,587,597,239   +24.9 % (= D$ share)
The D$ dominates: every load/store/PTW hit is one cycle longer.

I$ fetch buffer, riscv-tests caches + random latency (OREG=1 vs 0):
  only the last-doubleword buffer (first version)   +21.3 %
    same, I$ arrays forced unregistered              +2.4 %  (D$ share)
    same, D$ arrays forced unregistered              +18.9 % (I$ share)
  with the next-doubleword prefetch (this branch)   +8.8 %

== Bugs found on the way ==
- First fetch-buffer version answered a fetch accepted in the same cycle
  as inval_i (FENCE.I) from the buffer; icache_tb phase 8 caught it (2
  stale words). Fixed: the buffer is never used in an inval_i cycle.
- Verilator 5.020 rejects -GSRAM_OUT_REG=1 on a `bit` parameter
  (WIDTHTRUNC, 32-bit constant); the Makefiles pass 1'b1 / 1'b0.

== Round-1 review fix (PR #29 B1) ==
Bug: with SRAM_OUT_REG=1 a fetch accepted in S_IDLE as a hit on the
prefetched doubleword N, in the same cycle as a two-cycle-old prefetch
lookup (pf2_q && pf_hit) reloading N with another doubleword, was then
answered in S_FB from the new N (wrong word). Trigger: fetch X, a
non-sequential array hit, exactly one idle cycle, fetch X+8. The core's
fetch timing does not produce it (cycle counts below are unchanged),
but the synthesized configuration contains it.
Fix: no N capture in a cycle that accepts a fetch hitting N (one more
term in the N load enable).
Test: icache_tb gains ten "fetch-stream" phases (one fetch at a time
like the core, 0-3 idle cycles, mostly the next word or the doubleword
after the one before last; the reviewer's stress pattern) and an RNG
seed argument; `make -C sim icache` runs seeds 777, 1, 2.
  pre-fix RTL, OREG=1:  FAIL (wrong words from phase 10 on)
  fixed RTL: seeds 777, 1..10 x OREG 0/1: 22/22 PASS (230,000 checks each)
Gates after the fix:
  make lint (5.048) PASS 16 s; Verilator 5.020 (Docker): lint PASS, vec TB
    and OpenSBI+s_hello PASS with both settings, 864 s
  make core-test (both settings) PASS, 2,558 s (405 PASS lines; icache
    3 seeds x 2 settings; srammacro 36/36 x 2 families x 2 settings)
  riscv-tests 123/123 x {OREG 0,1} x {cached+random, uncached}, ~43 s each
  ACT 2,577/2,578 OREG=1 (699 s) and OREG=0 (650 s), only the waiver
  riscv-tests and ACT CSVs (per-test cycles) identical to the pre-fix run,
  so the earlier cycle-cost numbers and the Linux boot stand.
